---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config.js';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede={`How ${SITE.name} handles personal data.`}
  updated="29 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data this site collects, why, and what you can do about it. It is written to be read,
    not to be survived.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} ({SITE.url}) is the data controller for the personal data described here. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>

  <h3>When you just read the site</h3>
  <p>
    This is a static site. It sets no tracking cookies and embeds no advertising or social media trackers. Our hosting
    provider, Cloudflare, processes technical information inherent to serving a web page — your IP address, browser
    user agent, the page requested and the time — for delivery, security and abuse prevention. This is our legitimate
    interest in operating a functioning, non-abused website. We do not use it to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form or email us, we receive what you send: your name (if you give one), your email
    address, and the content of your message. We use it only to respond, and to keep a record of correction requests
    so that we can show why a profile changed. The lawful basis is our legitimate interest in answering enquiries and
    maintaining an accountable editorial record.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell or rent personal data.</li>
    <li>We do not run advertising or share data with ad networks.</li>
    <li>We do not use analytics that profile individual visitors across sites.</li>
    <li>We do not send marketing email. If you write to us, you get a reply, not a newsletter.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Processors we rely on</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, content delivery and security for this site.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — receiving and storing correspondence sent to our published addresses.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These providers process data on our instructions and under their own security obligations.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>General correspondence: normally up to 24 months, then deleted.</li>
    <li>
      Correction requests and the reasoning behind a resulting change: retained for as long as the profile is
      published, because a correction record that disappears is not a correction record.
    </li>
    <li>Server and security logs: retained by Cloudflare according to its own retention periods.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Personal data inside profiles</h2>
  <p>
    Some profiles are about people. That information is not collected from you — it is compiled from published,
    publicly available sources, and each claim is cited. We publish it in the public interest in maintaining an
    accurate, sourced record of documented public activity, and we limit profiles of living people to that public
    activity. See our <a href="/about/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for the limits we apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are the subject of a profile, you can ask us to correct inaccurate information, object to its publication,
    or request removal. Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and tell us which profile and which
    statements are at issue. We will respond, explain what a claim rests on, and correct or remove anything we cannot
    support.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access the personal data we hold about you, to have it
    corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict our processing, and to receive a copy in a portable format. To
    exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We aim to respond within 30 days
    and will not charge you for a reasonable request.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are in the UK, EU or another jurisdiction with a data protection authority, you also have the right to
    complain to it. We would rather you came to us first, but that right does not depend on doing so.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them. Note that profiles
    of institutions such as schools describe the institution, not individual pupils.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, the updated date above changes with it and the current version always appears
    on this page.
  </p>
</Page>
